              "text": "पंखा (pankhā) is a tadbhava, a word inherited from Sanskrit and reshaped by sound change. It comes from pakṣa, \"wing, feather; fan\" (CDIAL 7627). CDIAL notes the nasal and asks whether puṅkha, \"feathered end of an arrow\", crossed with it."
